<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="32f93547">&lt;p&gt;
    Document the details of each test case that includes the steps to be performed, pre-requisites (entry criteria), and
    the post-conditions (exit criteria) necessary to indicate a successful completion.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="a422bdc6"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="30bcfd6">&lt;p&gt;
    When performing this task, consider the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        When a scenario is tested, what would the result look like? This is the expected result of the test case.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are there any dependencies related to this case? Can the implementation of this test case run independently or are
        external inputs needed?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Are there any prerequisite conditions for a test case?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        What needs to be verified (e.g. does the application login function as expected)?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        What data is needed to perform the execution conditions?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        What actions need to be performed in each step (e.g. is login to an application required)?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        How should the action be performed (e.g. should the login window open followed by entering a username and
        password)?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        What is the result of the action performed (e.g. is the login successful)?
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Each step of the test case should consider the positive, negative, boundary and invalid values of the expected
        results to&amp;nbsp;confirm a&amp;nbsp;conclusive test.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="fb5956f8"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="146c4675">To provide standard, repeatable testing that validates the entire solution, including interfaces with external systems,
fulfills solution requirements.</attribute>
